.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: EUPL-1.2
.TH WAYLAND-SHARE-BRIDGE 1 "2026-11-18" "wayland-share-bridge @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wayland-share-bridge \- share Wayland screens and windows with X11 applications
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wayland-share-bridge
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B wayland-share-bridge
.B \-\-list-sources
.br
.B wayland-share-bridge
.RB [ \-\-reselect [= KIND ]]
.br
.B wayland-share-bridge
.B \-\-status
.br
.B wayland-share-bridge
.B \-\-quit
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wayland-share-bridge
captures a Wayland screen or window and paints every frame into an ordinary
X11 window.  X11 and XWayland applications (WPS Office, Zoom, Feishu, Electron
applications, browsers, OBS, ...) can capture that window like any other, even
though they cannot see native Wayland windows at all.
.PP
By default the bridge talks to the compositor directly through
.BR ext-image-copy-capture-v1 ;
screens are enumerated with
.BR wl_output
and windows with
.BR ext-foreign-toplevel-list-v1 .
The sources are offered in the tray menu, so switching between them is a
single click and no desktop portal picker is involved.
With
.BR \-\-portal
(or when the compositor lacks those protocols) the bridge falls back to the
.BR org.freedesktop.portal.ScreenCast
portal and the compositor's own picker.
.PP
The bridge window is invisible while it waits (via
.BR _NET_WM_WINDOW_OPACITY
or a compositor window rule) and click-through (empty XFixes input region).
A window shown with
.B \-\-show
or the tray entry accepts the pointer so it can be dragged, and hides itself
again when sharing stops.
The installed launcher
.B wayland-share-bridge-launch
adds the Hyprland rule that hides the window.
.PP
A single instance runs per session and offers a tray icon (StatusNotifierItem
with a D-BusMenu) plus a small control interface on the session bus.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-cursor= MODE
Cursor mode for the portal backend: \fBhidden\fR, \fBembedded\fR (default) or
\fBmetadata\fR (delivered as stream metadata, not painted by the mirror).
Direct capture paints the cursor for monitor sources.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-source\-kind= KIND
Fallback source kind for the portal backend: \fBauto\fR (default, remembers the
last choice), \fBany\fR, \fBscreen\fR or \fBwindow\fR.
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-source= SPEC
Capture SPEC immediately:
.BI screen: NAME
or
.BI window: APP_ID
or
.IB window: APP_ID | TITLE
or
.IB region: NAME , X , Y , W , H \fR.
Names are the ones printed by \fB\-\-list\-sources\fR.
The
.I region
form mirrors only that rectangle of the named screen and requires direct
capture.  When another instance is already running, SPEC switches that
instance instead of starting a second one.
.TP
.BR \-L ", " \-\-list\-sources
Print the screens and windows that can be shared, one per line as
.I kind:id<TAB>label\fR, then exit.  Exits with status 1 when the compositor
does not support direct capture (there is nothing to list then).
.TP
.B \-\-portal
Always use the desktop portal (system picker) instead of direct capture.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-remember
Remember the last source (default).  The state is stored in
.IR $XDG_STATE_HOME/wayland-share-bridge/state ;
the portal restore token (when returned) in
.IR $XDG_STATE_HOME/wayland-share-bridge/restore_token .
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no\-remember
Do not remember the source.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-show
Show the bridge window.  Intended for debugging; a shown window accepts the
pointer so it can be dragged, hide it again from the tray.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-title= TEXT
Window title.  Defaults to
.IR "Wayland Share Bridge" .
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-token\-file= PATH
Use a custom restore token file for the portal backend.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-tray
Do not create the tray icon.  The D-Bus control interface stays, so
\fB\-\-status\fR, \fB\-\-quit\fR, \fB\-\-reselect\fR and
\fB\-\-source\fR keep working.
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-multiple
Allow more than one running instance.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH TRAY MENU
The tray icon offers a categorised menu:
.TP
.B Stop sharing
Stop mirroring and hide the window again; the bridge keeps running.
.TP
.B Show/Hide shared window
Toggle the visibility of the mirror window on your own screen.  Hidden it is
invisible and click-through, shown it accepts the pointer so the compositor
can drag it.  The window hides itself again when sharing stops.
.TP
.B Screens
Submenu with one entry per monitor; the active source carries a checkmark.
.TP
.B Windows
Submenu grouped by application; each application has one entry per window, and
the active source carries a checkmark.  A
.B Search: QUERY (clear)
entry appears first while \fB\-\-search\fR is active.
.TP
.B Share via system portal...
Runs the portal picker (same as \fB\-\-reselect\fR).
.TP
.B Quit
Stops the bridge.
.PP
The running version is part of the menu header
.IR "wayland-share-bridge \fIVERSION\fR" ,
which tray hosts render from the StatusNotifierItem tooltip title.
The menu and the status text follow
.BR LC_ALL ", " LC_MESSAGES " and " LANG
(English or Chinese).
.PP
The source submenus are refreshed every time they are opened, and the SNI
tooltip shows the current sharing status.  dbusmenu has no text
input widget, so the window search is set with \fB\-\-search\fR (or the
SearchWindows control method) and cleared from the menu.
.SH CONTROLLING A RUNNING INSTANCE
.TP
.BR \-\-reselect [= KIND ]
Ask the portal for a new source, optionally restricted to
\fBKIND\fR (\fBany\fR, \fBscreen\fR or \fBwindow\fR).
.TP
.BR \-\-source= SPEC
Switch the running instance to SPEC (same syntax as the option above).
.TP
.B \-\-status
Print what the running instance is sharing and the version it runs.
.TP
.B \-\-quit
Stop the running instance.
.TP
.BR \-\-search= QUERY
Filter the Windows submenu of the running instance to windows whose app id,
title or identifier contains QUERY (case-insensitive).  An empty QUERY clears
the filter.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Ask the running instance to pick a new source through the portal.
.TP
.B SIGINT ", " SIGTERM
Stop the bridge.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
Compositor connection used for direct capture.
.TP
.B DISPLAY
X server connection (XWayland) used for the mirror window.
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
Base directory for the remembered source and the portal restore token.
.TP
.B WAYLAND_SHARE_BRIDGE_BINARY
Binary executed by the launcher (default:
.BR wayland-share-bridge ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/wayland-share-bridge/state
Remembered source (\fIsource=screen:NAME\fR, \fIsource=window:APP_ID|TITLE\fR
or \fIsource=region:NAME,X,Y,W,H\fR) and the remembered source kind for the
portal backend (\fIsource_kind=screen|window\fR).
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/wayland-share-bridge/restore_token
Portal restore token, when the portal returns one.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/wayland-share-bridge/bridge.log
Diagnostics of a bridge started from the desktop entry (the launcher
redirects stderr there; the file is truncated past 1 MiB).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B wayland-share-bridge-launch
Start the bridge from a desktop session and use the tray menu.
.TP
.B wayland-share-bridge --list-sources
See what can be shared, then pass one of the names to \fB\-\-source\fR.
.TP
.B wayland-share-bridge --source=screen:DP-2
Share the monitor called DP-2.
.TP
.B wayland-share-bridge --source=region:DP-2,100,200,1280,720
Share a 1280x720 rectangle at 100,200 of the monitor called DP-2.
.TP
.B wayland-share-bridge --source=window:firefox
Switch an already running instance to the firefox window.
.TP
.B wayland-share-bridge --no-tray --source='window:firefox|DeepSeek'
Share one window, run headless (no tray).
.TP
.B wayland-share-bridge --portal --cursor=hidden
Use the portal picker with the cursor hidden.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemd.exec (5),
.BR xdg-desktop-portal (1),
.BR pipewire (1),
.BR hyprctl (1)
.SH LICENSE
EUPL-1.2.  The original idea and the first implementation come from
video_bridge by lmarz; see the NOTICE file.
